course: dictionary
lesson: 7906
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the words around it show you which one the writer means. The word rat is a good example.
explain: «At dusk the Rat dresses everybody for the expedition: a belt, a sword, a cutlass, a pair of pistols...» Here Rat is the name of a character, an animal who acts like a person in a story. The clues dresses, expedition and sword show it is not a pest in a kitchen.
explain: Always ask: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense. «He ratted on his best friend» fits the meaning tell on someone, but not the meaning of a small furry animal.
fact: Rat is a noun: a rodent like a large mouse, with a long thin tail, sharp teeth and grey or brown fur.
fact: Informally, a rat is a nasty, mean or disloyal person.
fact: Rat on someone means to tell on them.
fact: «Rats!» is a mild word said when something goes wrong.
fact: In science, rats are clever and can learn mazes. Wild rats can carry germs, so don't touch them, and wash your hands after handling pet rats.
exercise: «Scientists found rats make high chirps when tickled.» What is a rat in this sentence? | A nasty, mean or disloyal person | *A rodent like a large mouse, with a long thin tail | To tell on someone | A mild word said when something goes wrong
exercise: Ella drops her ice cream and says, «Rats!» What does she mean? | A rodent with grey fur | *A mild word said when something goes wrong | She is telling on someone | A nasty person who is out to get her
exercise: «Don't rat on your friend, Sam.» What does rat on mean here? | Sing a song loudly | *Tell on someone | Run very fast | Hold someone's hand
test:
«Wild rats can carry germs, so keep food covered and bins closed.» Why should you keep bins closed? | *To stop rats and germs getting to the food | To keep the bin warm | Because bins are fun to open | To make the bin lighter
test:
«He is such a rat, he never shares.» What does rat mean here? | *A nasty, mean or disloyal person | A rodent with grey fur and sharp teeth | A mild word said when something goes wrong | To tell on someone
exam:
«When the offer seemed too good to be true, Maya began to smell a rat.» What does smell a rat mean? | *Suspect a trick | Smell something bad in the kitchen | Feel soaking wet like a drowned rat | Go to sleep early
